## =============================================================================
## .github/workflows/ci.yml.template — continuous integration (checks on every push/PR)
## =============================================================================
## GUIDE STEP   0.5 (lint, tests, audit, bandit), 4.3 (image job), 5.1 / 5.3
##              (PostgreSQL for the tests), 6.1 (Redis), 10.1 (PDF libraries)
## PURPOSE      GitHub Actions runs this workflow on a fresh virtual machine for
##              every push and pull request. Its jobs (each a separate machine):
##                lint        ruff (lint + format check) and mypy
##                tests       fast test suite (everything except the slow ABM tests)
##                tests-abm   the slow agent-based-model tests, in parallel
##                audit       pip-audit (known vulnerabilities in dependencies)
##                bandit      insecure patterns in te_platform/
##                image       build Dockerfile.platform and scan it with Trivy
##              With branch protection on `main` (guide 0.1), a PR can only be
##              merged when all jobs pass.
## WHY THE .template SUFFIX
##              GitHub reads every file in .github/workflows/ as a workflow. A
##              file that is entirely comments has no `on:` trigger, and GitHub
##              would report it as an invalid workflow on every push. Keeping the
##              suffix makes GitHub ignore it. ACTIVATION = uncomment, then
##              rename to ci.yml (git mv ci.yml.template ci.yml).
## USED BY      GitHub; branch protection rules (required checks).
## DEPENDS ON   uv.lock (guide 0.2), the [tool.ruff]/[tool.mypy] sections and
##              the dev extra of pyproject.toml (guide 0.3), Dockerfile.platform
##              (job `image`, 4.3), deploy/postgres/ and
##              te_platform/db/alembic.ini (the test database, 5.1 / 5.3).
## WHY          Guide §2.1-§2.2: quality and security checks that nobody can
##              forget, on a clean machine (no "works on my laptop").
## ACTIVATE     Uncomment the 0.5 code (commented once), rename, push a branch
##              and open a PR to see the checks run. Each later block
##              (commented twice, under a `## Guide X.Y` line) at its step.
##              Lint locally before pushing (actionlint is a linter for
##              workflow files):
##                docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/repo" -w /repo rhysd/actionlint:1.7.12
## ACTIONS      Third-party actions are pinned to a full commit SHA (the
##              version is in the comment next to it): a tag can be moved to
##              other code by whoever controls the action's repository, a
##              commit SHA cannot. Dependabot updates the SHA and the comment.
## =============================================================================

