## Guide 0.5
## [ ] 1. `name: CI` and the `on:` triggers: push to main, every
##        pull_request.
## [ ] 2. `permissions: contents: read` (least privilege for GITHUB_TOKEN)
##        and a `concurrency` group ci-${{ github.ref }} with
##        cancel-in-progress: true.
## [ ] 3. `jobs:` → `lint` on ubuntu-latest: checkout, setup-uv with the
##        cache keyed by uv.lock (both pinned to a commit SHA, see ACTIONS
##        above), then four `run:` steps:
##          | - run: uv sync --frozen --all-extras
##          | - run: uv run ruff check .
##        then `ruff format --check .` and `mypy te_platform`.
## [ ] 4. `tests`: the same three setup steps, then pytest -x ignoring the
##        ABM tests (--ignore-glob='tests/test_abm_*.py').
## [ ] 5. `tests-abm`: same setup, then pytest -x on tests/test_abm_*.py
##        only (a separate job runs in parallel; fast feedback first).
## [ ] 6. `audit`: checkout, setup-uv, `uv export --frozen --all-extras
##        --no-emit-project --no-hashes` into requirements-audit.txt, then
##        pip-audit on it, pinned, without pip (the list is already
##        complete, every version exact):
##          | uvx pip-audit@2.10.1 --disable-pip --no-deps \
##          |     -r requirements-audit.txt
## [ ] 7. `bandit`: checkout, setup-uv, `uvx bandit@1.9.4 -r te_platform -ll`.
## [ ] 8. Check: push a branch and open a PR; all jobs appear and must
##        pass, and a failing test blocks the merge.
##
## Guide 4.3 (Dockerfile.platform exists)
## [ ] 9. `image`: checkout, `docker build -f Dockerfile.platform -t
##        te-platform:ci .`, then aquasecurity/trivy-action on that image
##        with severity HIGH,CRITICAL, ignore-unfixed true, exit-code "1".
##
## Guide 5.1 / 5.3 (the database tests need a real PostgreSQL)
## [ ] 10. In `tests`: a job-level `env:` with TE_DATABASE_URL (the app
##        role) and TE_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL (the migration role) on
##        127.0.0.1:5432, and before pytest a step that writes the three
##        throw-away password files (db_admin_password, db_app_password,
##        db_migrator_password, readable by the container's postgres user)
##        into $RUNNER_TEMP/pg-secrets, starts postgres:16 with that folder
##        at /run/secrets, POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE and the repository's
##        deploy/postgres scripts (as compose.yml mounts them), and waits
##        for it:
##          | until docker exec te-ci-pg pg_isready -h 127.0.0.1 \
##          |     -U te_admin -d te; do sleep 1; done
##        (A GitHub `services:` container cannot be used here: it starts
##        before the checkout, so it cannot mount the init scripts.)
## [ ] 11. Guide 5.3: a step `uv run alembic -c te_platform/db/alembic.ini
##        upgrade head` after it.
##
## Guide 6.1 (Redis)
## [ ] 12. In `tests`: TE_REDIS_URL in the env, and a `services:` entry
##        redis:7 with port 6379 and a redis-cli ping health check.
##
## Guide 10.1 (PDF reports)
## [ ] 13. In `tests`, before pytest: apt-get install the WeasyPrint
##        libraries (libpango-1.0-0 libpangoft2-1.0-0 libharfbuzz0b).
## [ ] 14. Check after each block: actionlint (ACTIVATE above), then a PR.
